{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407991-help-building-a-water-aspect-immaculate-monk-investigator-criminal-sleuth","id":1407991,"title":"Help building a Water Aspect Immaculate Monk Investigator/Criminal sleuth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-13T11:32:15-07:00","id":1407991,"title":"Help building a Water Aspect Immaculate Monk Investigator/Criminal sleuth","content":"I am trying to go about optimizing a character gen for the character mentioned in the subject<br /> <br /> It has been some years since I've touched on Exalted and completely new to 3E, but I am very much liking the look of it<br /> <br /> I may have some wiggle room to use some exp to address a few shortfalls and weaknesses, ST discretion applied accordingly<br /> <br /> I'm gearing towards combat-oriented/optimized, stealthy, not explicitly assassin, kind of implicitly, but can just as easily fare in a straight-up fight, just very manoeuvrable and can suprise attack in the open relatively easily, but has the capacity for criminal abilities from House Iselsi coupled with invesgating capacity, to leverage the aspect abilities, specced in to Lore to utilize the specialty from the Cloister of Wisdom and used the 2nd specialty in Martial Arts, I'm just a bit unsure if the speccing in to Lore is worth the sacrifice to chargen Awareness<br /> <br /> Has started to see past some of the Immaculate Order philosophies and losing faith (will continue to do so, but still operate within it for personal objectives), knows of some handlings the Sidereals have had historically<br /> <br /> Would like to seek truth in Realm matters, historical and occulty affairs, but has yet to delve in to much of the Occulty side of things, (exp in future to be applied accordingly, with the Occult Martial arts too maybe?)<br /> <br /> I'm not wanting to go for Tiger Claws as weapons and would prefer reaper daiklaves, for Shining Point martial arts <br /> <br /> I have drafted up a points distribution without exp increases yet and I'm unsure where exactly to place some specialties<br /> <br /> I'm not too sure on where to go with starting charms either<br /> <br /> <br /> Water Aspect - Cloister of Wisdom<br /> <br /> <br /> Strength 1<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 5 <br /> <br /> Charisma 1 <br /> Manipulation 5 <br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 5<br /> Intelligence 3 <br /> Wits 1<br /> <br /> Water Aspect Abilities (and Specialities)<br /> <br /> Brawl 1<br /> --Martial Arts (Water Dragon Style) 5 (with specialty) (Cloister)<br /> --MA (Shining Point) 5<br /> Bureacracy<br /> Investigation 5 <br /> Larceny 5<br /> Sail <br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> <br /> Athletics 5<br /> Dodge 5<br /> Lore 5 (with specialty) (Cloister)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> Stealth 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: High Realm)<br /> <br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> Artifact 3 (Reaper Daiklaves)<br /> Mentor 3<br /> Danger Sense 3<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Backing (Immaculate Order) 2<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Old Realm) 1<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Contacts 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl/Martial Arts: Become The Hammer<br /> <br /> <br /> Starting Charms<br /> <br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d72<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d73<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d74<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d75","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26336-farrowin64","name":"Farrowin64","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:45:12-07:00","id":1408032,"title":"","content":"I think what you have is okay so far, but you\u2019re going to suffer in non-combat areas, and not be a really stellar assassin.<br /> <br /> With five ox bodies, and you really want Water Dragon up to the form for that immaculate ability to ignore terrestrial keywords, so that\u2019s 4 charms there. Then five single point charms at Essence 2 leaves you with one other charm, which you probably want to be Vanishing Wind Body if you want combat stealth. You will be amazingly deadly, but you won\u2019t have more than the excellency for investigation, resistance, larceny, etc. <br /> <br /> Assassins also really need a good join battle to launch an ambush on turn one, and your join battle right now is 1 with no magic to boost it.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re also a criminal investigator with no bureaucracy, a Sense Motive pool of 5, guile of 3, and a base resolve of 1, none of which can be boosted by magic. Not that you necessarily 100% need those to be an investigator, but you won\u2019t be the best sleuth you can be without them. <br /> <br /> <br /> The last thing is, if you\u2019re trying to optimize for combat, like truly optimize, then you\u2019re in for a long road that kind of precludes anything else for your character. There\u2019s so much stuff that\u2019s good to have that will make you more deadly in combat that if you don\u2019t make any compromises you won\u2019t really get to comfortably pick anything else until Essence 4 or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:32:11-07:00","id":1408045,"title":"","content":"I've had a bit of a re-jig of a few bits whilst waiting for some input and I don't anticipate to be the best sleuth/criminal, it's the more of the off-role to have whilst not in combat. I don't mind branching off a little bit and making a compromise here and there, just wanted to get a solid gen for combat optimized while still taking advantage of the Aspect abilities to some degree<br /> <br /> I take it that it's of high imperative to sink in to Resistance for the full 5 Oxbody<br /> <br /> <br /> Water Aspect - Cloister of Wisdom<br /> <br /> <br /> Strength 1<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 5<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 5<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Water Aspect Abilities (and Specialities)<br /> <br /> Brawl 1<br /> --Martial Arts (Water Dragon Style) 5 (with specialty) (Cloister)<br /> --MA (Shining Point) 5<br /> Bureacracy<br /> Investigation 5<br /> Larceny 5<br /> Sail<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> <br /> Athletics 5<br /> Dodge 5<br /> Lore 5 (with specialty) (Cloister)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> Stealth 5 (Surprise attacks)<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: High Realm)<br /> <br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> Danger Sense 3<br /> Eidetic Memory 2<br /> Natural Immunity 2<br /> Direction Sense 1<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Backing (Immaculate Order) 1<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Old Realm) 1<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Followers 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> Brawl/Martial Arts: Become The Hammer<br /> <br /> <br /> Starting Charms<br /> <br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d72<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d73<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d74<br /> Resistance: Oxbody Technique \u00d75","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26336-farrowin64","name":"Farrowin64","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:32:52-07:00","id":1408047,"title":"","content":"This character WILL die to an ambush. You over-optimized so far your min-maxing maximized your mins, your weaknesses are too pronounced. You're going to want to move some of that 5s so you can have some 3s where you have 0s now.<br /> Get awareness, get some wits, I wouldn't personally start with two MAs at 5 since that is just kneecapping your versatility. <br /> <br /> But if you want to go that route, do what DrLoveMonkey said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T17:18:22-07:00","id":1408077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Farrowin64</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407991-help-building-a-water-aspect-immaculate-monk-investigator-criminal-sleuth#post1407991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gearing towards combat-oriented/optimized, stealthy, not explicitly assassin, kind of implicitly, but can just as easily fare in a straight-up fight, just very manoeuvrable and can suprise attack in the open relatively easily, but has the capacity for criminal abilities from House Iselsi coupled with invesgating capacity, to leverage the aspect abilities, specced in to Lore to utilize the specialty from the Cloister of Wisdom and used the 2nd specialty in Martial Arts, I'm just a bit unsure if the speccing in to Lore is worth the sacrifice to chargen Awareness</div> </div> </div> </div>so just to be clear, your priorities are (in order) 1- a great fighter 2-a great stealther and 3-a goodish investigator. <br /> <br /> I agree with LoveMonkey and Cheshire Cat, 2 martial arts doesn't leave room for much else. I don't think even a Solar could shine jamming this much in to a single starting character. Do you NEED Water Dragon and Single Point? Do you need 5 Ox bodies? Taking that many ox bodies is overkill, even if you were just a dedicated fighter and nothing else. Especially if you plan to do Stealth, the exact last people who need extra HP (if your Stealth character is taking damage, you're already losing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T17:44:36-07:00","id":1408080,"title":"","content":"When you say \u201csolid gen for optimized combat\u201d do you mean like, an excellent fighter who can kill almost anything, or an unstoppable god of death who\u2019s utterly unmatched by anyone else in the world? Because 5s in all combat relevant stats and stating with two MAs and 5 ox bodies is much more the later. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407991-help-building-a-water-aspect-immaculate-monk-investigator-criminal-sleuth?p=1408047#post1408047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This character WILL die to an ambush.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 22 health levels I don\u2019t really see it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T02:19:24-07:00","id":1408117,"title":"","content":"I recently built a Water Aspect Single Point Stylist...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Burano Zena<br /> Water Aspect<br /> Dragon Princess<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 5<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 1<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Water Aspect Abilities (and Specialities)<br /> <br /> Brawl 1<br /> Martial Arts: Water Dragon Style 5<br /> Martial Arts: Single Point Shining Into the Void 5 (Stormcaller)<br /> Bureaucracy 0<br /> Investigation 0<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Sail 1<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Dodge 5 (Armored)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Resistance 5 (Sword-in-hand)<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> Integrity 3 (The Pure Way)<br /> Linguistics 1<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Rivertongue)<br /> <br /> Artifact 5 (Stormcaller)<br /> Artifact 3 (Medium Armor - Enchanted Leathers)<br /> Cult 3<br /> Martial Artist 4<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Language (Dragon-tongue)<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> (Dragon Caste Freebie) Resources 3<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Brawl/MA: Become the Hammer<br /> 4. Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> 5. Resistance: Purifying Blood Ascendancy<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Soaring Leap Technique<br /> 2. Water Dragon Style: Flowing Water Defense<br /> 3. Water Dragon Style: Rippling Water Strike<br /> 4. Water Dragon Style: Drowning-In-Blood Technique<br /> 5. Water Dragon Style: Water Dragon Form<br /> 6. Single Point: Cutting Light Concentration<br /> 7. Single Point: Shining Starfall Execution<br /> 8. Single Point: Single Point Shining Into The Void Form<br /> 9. Single Point: Fatal Stroke Flash<br /> 10. Single Point: Liquid Steel Flow<br /> 11. Single Point: Void Slicing Wind<br /> 12. Resistance: Oxbody Technique<br /> 13. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x2<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> 14. Stormcaller: Fulminating Edge Flash<br /> 15. Stormcaller: Storm Binding<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> <br /> Defining Principle: I am a student of cutting<br /> Defining Principle: Demons must be controlled<br /> Major Principle: The Pure Way (Loyal Adherence)<br /> Defining Tie: Clan Benaro (Loyalty)<br /> Major Tie: The people of Prasad (Nobless Oblige)<br /> Minor Tie: Anathema (Disgust)<br /> <br /> Evasion 5 (+3, 6m; +1 non-Charm 3m)<br /> Parry 7 (+3, 6m)<br /> Soak 9 Hardness 7<br /> Mobility Penalty -1<br /> <br /> Stormcaller Attacks: Accuracy 14 (11 Decisive)(+5, and reroll 6s on damage, 5m), Damage 15 (Overwhelming 5), Lethal, Stormy<br /> <br /> Chakram Attacks: Accuracy 9/8/7 (5 Decisive), 10 Damage (OVR 1), Lethal, Cutting, Mounted<br /> <br /> Join Battle 11 (+3 to result)(+3 successes, 6m)<br /> Rush 10 (+6 dice, exploding 10s, 6m)<br /> Disengage 10 (+6 dice, 6m; +1 non-Charm success 3m)<br /> <br /> Resolve 4 (5)<br /> Guile 1<br /> <br /> Willpower 6<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (21, 10 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -2 x6<br /> -4 x1<br /> Incap<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She's not a Dynast nor an investigator. But she's fair to middling at killing Solars one-on-one: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368113#post1368113\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...13#post1368113</a><br /> <br /> I hope that helps? That's about as combat optimized as a Single Point Deeb gets. (That said, I'd love to test her out against your 5 Ox-Body monster there!)<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Honestly, you should really talk to your ST about your level of combat prowess. Exalted really starts to break down at the optimized end. It works WAY better when you have your dots spread out all over the place.<br /> <br /> 1E expected every Dynast to have 2 dots in Archery, Brawl (or Martial Arts), Melee, Performance, Presence, Ride, Lore and Socialize. Having less than that marked you as some deficient outcast. I find it's helpful to build according to those minimums, then reduce the stats based on what your character is bad at. Archery 0 doesn't just mean you never studied Archery (you will have studied Archery as a child), it means you actively suck at Archery. Then I'd bring up to 2 any stats you studied at secondary school or use for your job (Awareness, Larceny, Beurocracy, Investigation, Stealth). Then take anything you want to be good at to 3 dots. Then spend BP to meet your Charm minimums.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, this is probably the weakest way you could build a character. The character creation mini-game actively punishes you for building this way. But it's the way that (if everyone in your group follows suit) works best in actual play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-14-2020, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:39:25-07:00","id":1408136,"title":"","content":"I feel any build that can use it gets a whole point up the ladder of optimization if they take Stormcaller. The fact that its a match for SP just makes it even more minmaxxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T09:30:48-07:00","id":1408178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407991-help-building-a-water-aspect-immaculate-monk-investigator-criminal-sleuth?p=1408136#post1408136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel any build that can use it gets a whole point up the ladder of optimization if they take Stormcaller. The fact that its a match for SP just makes it even more minmaxxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that build is from my pre-No Artifact 5s period.<br /> <br /> Works almost as well with Shining Ice Mirror (so long as Deebs are deemed Ressonant).<br /> <br /> Zena Dragon Princess exists more to illustrate how difficult it is to optimize a DB with Single Point than a sample of a character you should play. Thus far she's the only combat optimized DB I've made who's lost a fight to Volfer. Trying to tag criminal, investigator, monk, assassin onto that is perfectly doable at the default level of play. But combat optimized? It's going to be tight.<br /> <br /> I would strongly encourage folks not to min-max their Exalted for combat. But if you really want to do it... that's how you do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:51:40-07:00","id":1408233,"title":"","content":"I'm also in firm agreement with JohnDoe. Exalted isn't like DnD where the game totally works well if all the players max their primary stat and take combat optimal choices. Fighting a Beholder and his lair at level 9 absolutely works if your fighter has 20 strength, heavy armor and a magic sword, and thebard has 20 charisma, 16 dex, and Fireball.<br /> <br /> For Exalted on the other hand, if everyone in your party optimizes for combat, your Storyteller has to throw out almost every single enemy in the book, and more often than not instead of having kinetic action fight scenes you'll just skip it and move on. <br /> <br /> A really optimized combat character can work well sometimes, but usually only in groups where not everyone is like that. Like if you're the Dawn, for example, and you are really combat optimized, but the rest of your circle isn't. When you guys get into a combat scene YOU are basically invincible, and don't have to worry about the enemy attacks, but you actually do have to push yourself to protect your friends.<br /> <br /> Which seems like a game about the Dawn and his cheerleader squad, but only if theres no serious non-combat threats. Like if a manse is about to explode and kill not only the entire party but the city above as well, and the only way to stop it is to decipher this ancient language that the manual was written in, now all of a sudden the linguistics guy saves everyone else. <br /> <br /> The even better way to do it is by having the Dawn fight off the manse's automatraon guardians WHILE the linguistics guy is deciphering the code, with like an extended roll with a terminus of three, duration one round, something like that, but that's for another thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a side benefit about building your dynast as John suggests too, and that's if your ST sticks to the difficulty guidelines in the book, you're going to be pretty damn capable at anything that you even have 2-3 dots in. Like dex 5 and ride 2, you're going to be able to ride a horse across a two foot plank spanning two buildings 90% of the time or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:58:41-07:00","id":1410333,"title":"","content":"Thank you all greatly for your input.<br /> <br /> I have discussed with the others in the group 